      "id": "ma-blue-envelope-autistic-drivers-statewide-2026",
      "text": "blue envelope program expands statewide support for autistic drivers the free, voluntary envelopes give autistic motorists a recognizable way to share documents and communication guidance during traffic stops. massachusetts has launched a statewide blue envelope program intended to make traffic stops safer and clearer for autistic drivers and passengers. the free, voluntary envelope can hold a driver’s license, vehicle registration and emergency-contact card. its exterior provides communication guidance for law-enforcement officers, while a qr code offers additional information. drivers may keep the envelope on a sun visor or in another visible, accessible place and hand it to an officer during an interaction. the program became state law in june and expanded availability at registry of motor vehicles locations beginning september 1. envelopes are also available through state police barracks and participating local police departments, with mail requests offered through the statewide program. using an envelope is optional and does not change a driver’s legal obligations during a stop. its purpose is to reduce anxiety and help both the motorist and officer recognize communication needs before misunderstanding escalates. families and drivers should keep the documents inside current and check the state’s program page for locations and request instructions. massachusetts massachusetts massachusetts ma boston massachusetts blue envelope autism traffic stops massachusetts"
