      "text": "osterville man pleads not guilty after officer struck outside hyannis concert prosecutors say a speeding pickup hit a barnstable officer directing traffic sunday; the officer underwent surgery and his condition was not released. a 43-year-old osterville man pleaded not guilty monday after prosecutors accused him of driving drunk and striking a barnstable police officer outside a concert in hyannis, whdh reported. robert brando-hunt faces charges of operating under the influence of liquor as a second offense, operating under the influence with serious injury and negligence, and negligent operation of a motor vehicle. the case was heard in barnstable district court. police and prosecutors said the crash happened around 10:05 p.m. sunday on west main street after a zz top concert at the cape cod melody tent. they allege a black pickup was traveling at a high rate of speed when it entered a marked crosswalk and hit the officer, who was directing pedestrian traffic. prosecutors said the officer was wearing a reflective jacket and holding a flashlight in an illuminated crosswalk with flashing lights. they also alleged that brando-hunt’s blood-alcohol level was nearly three times the legal limit; that allegation has not been tested at trial. the officer was taken first to cape cod hospital and then transferred to a boston hospital, where he underwent surgery. his condition had not been released. brando-hunt’s bail was set at $10,000 cash, and he is due back in court in october. massachusetts massachusetts massachusetts ma hyannis hyannis, massachusetts massachusetts cape cod hyannis police"
