      "text": "two men charged after cranston cooking-oil theft a license-plate reader alert led officers to a van carrying about 100 gallons of used restaurant oil, police said. cranston police arrested two new york men early friday after officers recovered about 100 gallons of used cooking oil that authorities say had been taken from a local restaurant. anyeson veras martinez, 26, and steven velez toribio, 29, were each charged with larceny under $1,500. police said a flock license-plate reader alerted officers at 1:57 a.m. to a white 2018 ford transit with a pennsylvania plate associated with cooking-oil thefts. a second alert placed the van near route 37. an officer located it at pj's pub on pontiac avenue and stopped it at about 2:20 a.m. according to police, the van smelled of cooking oil and contained residue, two large containers, a hose and a pump. investigators estimated the recovered oil's value at about $200. used restaurant oil can be processed into biofuel and other products, giving it a resale value that has made storage tanks a theft target. the charges are allegations, and both men are presumed innocent unless proven guilty. police did not immediately say whether the case is connected to other reported thefts. rhode-island rhode-island rhode island ri cranston cranston, ri cranston cooking oil larceny license plate reader rhode island"
