      "text": "johnston parents rally as school-bus delays and long rides continue families say communication and routing problems persist weeks after the district began working with a new transportation provider. johnston parents rallied outside town hall ahead of a school committee meeting, saying students continue to face long rides, delays and limited communication under the district’s new bus provider. wjar reported that families have raised concerns about zum since the school year began. district and company officials have said service is improving, but parents at the rally said the changes have not gone far enough. some middle-school students said they must wake up especially early because their buses first transport high-school students. other students have arrived well before class and waited in school gymnasiums for as long as an hour after the district separated routes serving two elementary schools. the dispute is now about more than isolated late buses: families want clear responsibility, dependable pickup times and direct updates when routes change. the school committee and provider have not announced a final resolution. performance over the coming days will show whether route adjustments reduce delays or whether johnston needs a broader transportation plan. new-england ri johnston, rhode island rhode island johnston schools transportation"
