    "ri-record-early-voting-primary-2026": {
      "excerpt": "More than 37,000 voters cast ballots before Election Day, more than doubling the state’s previous primary-year benchmark.",
      "id": "ri-record-early-voting-primary-2026",
      "text": "rhode island primary sets record for early in-person voting more than 37,000 voters cast ballots before election day, more than doubling the state’s previous primary-year benchmark. rhode island entered primary day with a record 37,444 early in-person ballots cast, according to final figures reported tuesday by rhode island current from the department of state. the total, recorded as of 4 p.m., was more than twice the roughly 16,900 early in-person votes cast in the 2022 primary and more than triple the approximately 12,100 recorded in 2024. rhode island first offered early in-person voting in 2020 under pandemic-era rules that were later made permanent; just over 7,000 people used the option that year. the surge came ahead of high-profile democratic contests, including the gubernatorial rematch between gov. dan mckee and helena foulkes and the providence mayoral primary between brett smiley and david morales. early voting totals measure how people voted, not which candidates they supported, so the record does not by itself point to an outcome. it does show that a substantially larger share of the electorate chose to vote before tuesday, a change that can affect campaign strategy, staffing and the pace at which election officials process ballots. new-england ri rhode island rhode island elections early voting primary"
    },
    "ri-regent-seaglider-first-crewed-flight-2026": {
      "excerpt": "The North Kingstown company’s Viceroy prototype carried two captains in a brief ground-effect flight that begins the final stage of sea trials.",
      "id": "ri-regent-seaglider-first-crewed-flight-2026",
      "text": "regent seaglider completes first crewed flight on narragansett bay the north kingstown company’s viceroy prototype carried two captains in a brief ground-effect flight that begins the final stage of sea trials. north kingstown-based regent has completed the first crewed flight of its viceroy seaglider prototype on narragansett bay, moving the hybrid marine aircraft into the final stage of sea trials. two captains were aboard during the test, according to the company. regent said the prototype traveled 1,956 feet in ground-effect flight, reaching 33 feet above the water during a 30-second airborne segment. the craft is designed to operate in three modes: floating from a dock, rising onto hydrofoils and then flying close to the water, where ground effect can reduce aerodynamic drag. regent is developing the platform for coastal passenger service, cargo transport and defense missions. the milestone does not mean the vehicle is ready for commercial passengers. the company said continued testing will focus on refining performance, reducing operational risk and demonstrating readiness for future service. even so, carrying crew through the full transition from waterborne operation to flight marks a substantial engineering step for a rhode island company building a new class of coastal transportation on narragansett bay. rhode-island rhode-island rhode island ri north kingstown narragansett bay, rhode island regent narragansett bay seaglider north kingstown"
    },
    "ri-republican-governor-primary-guckian-pelino-close-2026": {
      "excerpt": "State election officials certified the Sept. 9 primary after reviews of three close contests left their outcomes unchanged; turnout topped 20%.",
      "id": "ri-republican-governor-primary-guckian-pelino-close-2026",
      "text": "rhode island certifies aaron guckian as gop governor nominee state election officials certified the sept. 9 primary after reviews of three close contests left their outcomes unchanged; turnout topped 20%. the rhode island board of elections certified aaron guckian as the republican nominee for governor tuesday after reviews of three close primary contests did not change any winner, rhode island current reported. a rereading of voting-machine flash drives left guckian’s margin over elaine pelino unchanged at 259 votes. reviews also preserved justin roias’ providence city council ward 4 victory, while a hand recount widened juan pichardo’s ward 9 margin from nine votes to 11. the board certified all sept. 9 primary results. the 158,973 ballots cast represented just over 20% of registered voters, the highest rhode island state-primary participation rate in a decade, according to historical election data cited by rhode island current. guckian advances to the nov. 3 general election against democratic nominee helena buonanno foulkes and independent candidates ken block, jay gotra and c.d. reynolds. pelino has continued to question the review process but the certified result determines the republican ballot line. rhode-island rhode-island rhode island ri providence rhode island aaron guckian elaine pelino governor rhode island primary"
    },
