      "id": "ri-uri-fall-classes-17000-students-2026",
      "text": "more than 17,000 uri students begin fall classes the semester starts after a move-in weekend that brought roughly 5,400 residential students to the kingston campus. more than 17,000 university of rhode island students begin fall classes wednesday after several days of move-in and orientation activities on the kingston campus, the university said. about 5,400 students moved into more than two dozen campus residence halls from september 4 through september 7. another roughly 600 are living in greek life houses, while about 100 are in the grandin international engineering, texas instruments and talent development achievement houses. hundreds of faculty, staff and student volunteers helped families unload during move-in weekend. the university’s orientation schedule, known as o-week, ran from september 4 through september 8 and included hundreds of events designed to introduce students to campus programs and one another. the opening-day milestone shifts the campus from arrival logistics to regular academic operations. for first-year students, the week included an official class welcome from president marc parlange, a class photograph on the quad and student activities such as rhodyfest. uri’s enrollment and housing figures also illustrate the scale of daily transportation, dining and student-service demands as the 2026–27 academic year gets underway. rhode-island rhode-island rhode island ri kingston kingston, ri university of rhode island students fall semester kingston"
    },
    "ri-uri-fine-arts-center-opening-2026-09-14": {
      "excerpt": "A ribbon-cutting marked the opening of a renovated arts facility and a new three-story academic building on Monday.",
      "id": "ri-uri-fine-arts-center-opening-2026-09-14",
      "text": "uri opens $99 million fine arts center renovation in kingston a ribbon-cutting marked the opening of a renovated arts facility and a new three-story academic building on monday. the university of rhode island celebrated the opening of its renovated fine arts center on monday with a ribbon-cutting ceremony in kingston, nbc 10 reported. university leaders, students, elected officials and community members gathered outside the robert e. will theatre on the kingston campus. an open house and guided tours followed the ceremony. the $99 million project included renovations to the 58-year-old fine arts center and construction of a new 71,000-square-foot, three-story academic building. the expansion includes a theater lobby, an art gallery and classrooms. new spaces are dedicated to digital art and media, while recording studios and other rooms support artists, designers, composers, performers and scholars. the building is open for classes this semester. the project was paid for through state capital funds, university funding and a bond approved by rhode island voters in 2021. uri also dedicated a choral room to the late rhode island senate president dominick j. ruggerio. rhode-island rhode-island rhode island ri kingston kingston, rhode island rhode island uri kingston arts and culture"
    },
