      "id": "tech-apple-iphone-duo-foldable-2026",
      "text": "apple unveils $1,999 foldable iphone duo the company’s first folding phone opens to a 7.6-inch display and leads its first major product event under ceo john ternus. apple introduced its first foldable phone wednesday, unveiling the $1,999 iphone duo at the company’s annual product event. the device opens like a passport to reveal a horizontal 7.6-inch screen and includes a smaller display on the outside. the duo uses apple’s a20 chip and c2 modem. the larger interior display is designed to run multiple windows, giving the company a new format for productivity and media while placing it directly into a foldable-phone segment already served by several rivals. apple also demonstrated a redesigned siri that it said will work with about 300,000 apps at release. the company announced updated conventional phones, with the iphone 18 pro starting at $1,199 and the pro max at $1,299, as well as $129 airpods. the launch was the first major hardware event led by chief executive john ternus. the duo’s high price and durability will be central tests as apple asks buyers to adopt a new form factor rather than a routine slab-phone upgrade. tech tech tech ca cupertino cupertino, ca apple iphone duo smartphones consumer technology"
    },
