      "text": "apple’s $1,999 iphone duo tests the foldable market apple is pitching its first folding phone as a premium personal ai device, but analysts question how broad the audience will be at its launch price. apple’s first foldable phone, the iphone duo, will start at $1,999 in the united states, placing it at the high end of an already small smartphone segment. the largest-storage version is priced at $3,199. apple demonstrated apps including zoom, slack and netflix using the expanded display and positioned the device as a personal hub for artificial intelligence. the launch gives apple a new form factor but leaves a central question about the size of the audience willing to pay the premium. idc expects foldables to account for less than 3% of global smartphone shipments in 2026 and 2027. counterpoint research estimated apple could sell about 6 million units by year-end, roughly a quarter of the foldable segment. samsung currently holds about 40% of the foldable market, giving apple an established rival and a benchmark for durability, software and everyday usefulness. omdia projects 22.3 million foldable shipments worldwide this year. apple’s entry could expand consumer awareness, but its initial price means the duo’s early performance will test whether large-screen multitasking and ai features are compelling enough to move foldables beyond a niche. tech tech tech california cupertino cupertino, california apple iphone duo foldable phones smartphones consumer technology"
    },
    "tech-apple-september-event-2026": {
      "excerpt": "The September 9 showcase is expected to introduce new iPhones and could offer the first public look at Apple’s next hardware strategy.",
      "id": "tech-apple-september-event-2026",
      "text": "apple set for first major product event under new ceo the september 9 showcase is expected to introduce new iphones and could offer the first public look at apple’s next hardware strategy. apple is scheduled to hold its fall product event wednesday, the company’s first major launch presentation under chief executive john ternus. reuters reported that apple is expected to introduce its next iphone lineup and may unveil a long-anticipated foldable model. the company had confirmed the september 9 event date but had not preannounced the devices, so product names, specifications and prices circulating before the presentation remain expectations rather than confirmed facts. ternus, apple’s longtime hardware chief, became ceo september 1 as tim cook moved to executive chairman. that leadership change puts unusual attention on how the event frames apple’s hardware priorities and its approach to artificial intelligence on consumer devices. a foldable phone would place apple in a segment already served by several rivals and could lift average selling prices, but demand will depend on durability, software and cost. the event itself will determine which reports were accurate. customers considering an upgrade should wait for apple’s published specifications and availability details rather than treating advance reports as final. tech tech tech ca cupertino cupertino, california apple iphone john ternus consumer technology"
