      "excerpt": "Silver Lake will remain the controlling shareholder of a combined European business-software group expected to close in 2027.",
      "id": "tech-cegid-silae-euro-10-billion-merger-2026",
      "text": "cegid and silae plan €10 billion software merger silver lake will remain the controlling shareholder of a combined european business-software group expected to close in 2027. french business-software provider cegid and payroll platform silae plan to merge in a transaction valuing the combined group at more than 10 billion euros, or about $11.6 billion, reuters reported wednesday. private-equity firm silver lake is the majority owner of both companies and will remain the controlling shareholder after the combination. the companies said newly appointed chief executive christian pedersen will lead the merged business, which is expected to bring together payroll, finance and other management-software products. the deal is scheduled to close in the first half of 2027, subject to the required reviews and transaction conditions. until those steps are completed, cegid and silae remain separate businesses and the timetable could change. the proposed merger would create a larger european software company serving businesses that increasingly want cloud-based tools for essential administrative work. scale can help software providers spread product-development and compliance costs, but integration will determine whether customers see simpler services or added complexity. the announcement establishes the strategic direction; execution will take place over the coming months. tech tech tech international paris france cegid silae software mergers"
