      "text": "deepseek taps citic securities for shanghai ipo preparations sources say the chinese ai startup has selected the brokerage for work ahead of a possible star market listing, though final terms remain undecided. chinese artificial-intelligence startup deepseek has selected citic securities to prepare for a domestic initial public offering, according to two people familiar with the matter cited by reuters. the company is working toward a possible listing on shanghai’s technology-focused star market. selecting an adviser and beginning pre-listing preparation moves the process forward, but it is not the same as filing a final prospectus or setting an offer date. deepseek became a prominent competitor in generative ai by developing models designed to use computing resources efficiently. a public listing could provide additional capital for computing infrastructure, model development and hiring as competition for researchers and hardware intensifies. important terms remain unsettled, including timing, valuation and the amount of stock to be sold. deepseek and citic securities had not publicly confirmed a final transaction in the initial report. any eventual offering would also require regulatory review. the current development is therefore a preparatory step, not a completed ipo or a publicly traded share price. tech international hangzhou, china deepseek citic securities artificial intelligence ipo"
    },
